# Generated analysis output. Only promoted, verified bundles are committed, and
# they are committed explicitly with `git add -f` after the release gates pass.
_targets/
# A previous run's store, kept aside so a rerun cannot silently reuse it
# and the audited bundle stays recoverable without a checkout.
_targets_archive_*/
bayesian/results/_staging/
bayesian/results/**/draws/

# Compiled Stan executables. The .stan source is the artefact; the binary is
# machine-specific and large.
bayesian/stan/masem_valid
bayesian/stan/*.exe
bayesian/stan/*.o
bayesian/stan/*.hpp

# Full posterior draws and fitted objects. These are NOT deposited anywhere: no
# archive location or checksum exists, and an earlier version of this file
# claimed otherwise. Exact verification of the reported diagnostics therefore
# requires rerunning the models from the pinned environment, which the fit
# ledger's per-fit seeds make deterministic. Depositing them is an open item in
# the pull request.
#
# What IS committed, because it is small enough to version, is the complete SBC
# record: diagnostics/sbc_ranks_raw.csv carries every truth, rank and
# per-replicate diagnostic, so the calibration audit can be recomputed exactly
# without refitting 600 models.
*.rds
*.csv.gz

# renv library. The lockfile is committed; the library is not.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/

# Editor and platform noise
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
*~

# Corrected source workbooks. Departures from the upstream files are expressed
# in data/provenance/corrections.csv and data/provenance/quality_scores.csv, so
# no modified binary is committed.
data/corrected/
